    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="1042" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1951v05/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">887.00 TA/1–2651: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Lebanon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bruins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d575-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-26T18:00:00-05:00">January 26, 1951—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>517. ReDeptel 501 Jan 24.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d575-f2"/> Dept continues believe
                    early signature FCN Treaty and Point Four General Agreement wld be excellent
                    practicable means strengthening US-Leb relations. Point Four Program for Leb can
                    be implemented only after Leb signs General Agreement.</p>
                <p>Suggest you discussing foregoing with Leb Govt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d575-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d575-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Harlan B. Clark, Officer in Charge of Lebanon–Syria–Iraq Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d575-f2" n="2" xml:id="d575-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it treated the subject of Communist aggression in Korea.
                    (693.95/1–1851)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
